module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.declared_confinement_the_host_cannot_start

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { AtCeiling, FoundOnRung, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { MechanicallyPreventable, Mitigatable }

data declared_confinement_the_host_cannot_start: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "declared_confinement_the_host_cannot_start" as NonEmptyStr,
  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundOnRung { rung: Mitigatable }, standing: AtCeiling { rung: MechanicallyPreventable, ceiling_reason: "mechanically preventable." as NonEmptyStr } },

  receipts: [
    "**A workload declares a confinement mode that its host cannot build, and nothing reads that before the workload is selected, so the first observation of the deficit is the workload's own failure.** INVALID STATE: a selection admits a run whose declared execution environment -- here Cursor's sandbox, which gunbc.cursor_harness_credential cursor_worker_turn_run declares as CursorSandboxEnabled so that --force is not unconfined -- cannot be constructed on the host the run is placed on. The run fails closed, which is right, but only AFTER selection: the attempt, its receipt-qualified credential snapshot, its launch and its child are all spent to learn a host fact that a free read answers without a provider call.",
    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS. It is not sandbox_properties_declared_but_not_enforced_by_the_realization: there the confinement is silently DROPPED and the workload runs unconfined while every observable reads confined (below the ladder). Here the realization refuses loudly. The two share a host cause -- kernel.apparmor_restrict_unprivileged_userns=1 on Ubuntu 24.04 (extdeps.linux.apparmor_userns), which blocks the unprivileged user namespace both the systemd user manager and Cursor's sandbox need -- and that shared cause is the reason to read the host fact once, by an observation, rather than let each consumer discover it. Nor is it suppressed_precondition_failure_runs_the_workload_unconstrained, whose precondition fails and whose diagnostic is thrown away. Here the diagnostic arrives, but too late. That row IS the hazard a naive repair walks into, though: disabling the sandbox to make the turn run would trade this class for that one.",
    "SPECIMEN, srv2, 2026-10-16 (Ubuntu 24.04.4, AppArmor 4.0.1, cursor-agent 2026.09.15-d2fe57e). With the custody key exported from its file inside sh, `cursor-agent status --format json` answered isAuthenticated true. The one-word turn `--print --output-format stream-json --model auto --mode ask --sandbox enabled --trust` then exited 1 before any provider request: 'Sandbox mode is enabled but not available on this system. Sandbox failed to start, possibly due to AppArmor configuration.' The free preflight `cursor-agent sandbox run printenv CURSOR_SANDBOX` reproduces it exactly, with exit 1 and stdout 'SandboxUnsupportedError ... Landlock error ... Failed to write /proc/self/uid_map (mapping UID 0 -> 1000): Operation not permitted ... Bubblewrap error: ... (same)'. `unshare -Ur true` on the same host is refused EPERM. Every production Cursor worker turn on srv2 would have failed this way after selection.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable. The failure occurred and was contained only by the CLI refusing to run unsandboxed; nothing before selection read the host. RUNG NOW: mechanically preventable, at a stated boundary. gunbc.worker_turn_standing cursor_standing_from_readings joins the preflight reading into the Cursor standing, so selection refuses with the host's cause BEFORE LAUNCH OR PROVIDER CONTACT -- AFTER the attempt's receipt-qualified snapshot has been acquired (gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_dispatch_actuator cursor_selection_observed takes it first), and the refused selection discards that snapshot. It holds only while the preflight executes on every draw. Moving the host-only preflight ahead of credential_register_then_take would also spare the snapshot; that is a further step, not claimed here. READY REQUIRES A DISCRIMINATING READ BY THE SUBJECT: the preflight's outer process sets CURSOR_SANDBOX to a gunbc sentinel (gunbc.cursor_harness_credential cursor_sandbox_discriminating_preflight_command), so only a real sandbox can make the command print native. Cursor documents injecting native into sandboxed children and falling back to approval-before-run when the sandbox is missing, but not that the variable is absent outside, so exit 0 alone, or an inherited native, could otherwise read as Ready over an unsandboxed run.",
    "CEILING: mechanically preventable. Whether a host can build a namespace sandbox is an external, mutable kernel and security-policy fact, so it is a boundary obligation observed per host (DESIGN section 4b), never a structural guarantee: a sysctl or an AppArmor profile can change under a converged host. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, a capability: a host standing that carries sandbox readiness as an observation attributed to the converge run that placed the confinement it depends on (for srv2, the pinned root-owned Cursor realization with its exact AppArmor profile), so selection reads one attributed host fact instead of each draw re-deriving it, and a host whose readiness has no placing run refuses (gunbc.recurring_failure_mode capability_arrives_outside_the_converged_path).",
    "WHAT DOES NOT CLIMB IT: an AppArmor profile attached to a user-writable, self-updating path (Cursor's own cursor-sandbox-apparmor package attaches to /home/*/.local/share/cursor-agent/versions/*/cursorsandbox, and on AppArmor 4 ships with `userns,` commented out), which would authorize whatever program later occupies the glob; lifting kernel.apparmor_restrict_unprivileged_userns host-wide; and CursorSandboxDisabled, which makes --force unconfined.",
  ],
  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "extdeps.llm.cursor_cli", decl_name: "cursor_sandbox_preflight_command", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.cursor_harness_credential", decl_name: "cursor_sandbox_preflight_reading", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.cursor_harness_credential", decl_name: "cursor_sandbox_discriminating_preflight_command", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.cursor_harness_credential", decl_name: "cursor_worker_turn_run", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.worker_turn_standing", decl_name: "cursor_standing_from_sandbox_refusal", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "extdeps.linux.apparmor_userns", decl_name: "apparmor_restrict_unprivileged_userns_sysctl_name", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
